WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.848 --> 00:00:07.172
Carrying my plot inventor, I walked to the front of the classroom.

2
00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:10.615
"It looks like a box," said Jake.

3
00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:14.779
"It is a box," I said.

4
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.865
"But because of what's in it, it's also something really cool—a plot inventor."

5
00:00:31.885 --> 00:00:35.729
"Oh boy someone muttered.

6
00:00:35.749 --> 00:00:39.973
"It's another one of Iggy's incredible inventions."

7
00:00:43.716 --> 00:00:44.557
in the box?"

8
00:00:45.057 --> 00:00:46.138
Gina wanted to know.

9
00:00:46.158 --> 00:00:51.964
"Something that will make writing a story really easy," I explained.

10
00:00:53.184 --> 00:00:54.845
"Lots of words and pictures.

11
00:00:55.285 --> 00:00:56.946
All you have to do is shake the box."

12
00:00:58.787 --> 00:01:01.569
Everyone watched while I gave the box a good shake.

13
00:01:01.589 --> 00:01:07.793
"Then you turn it over and let a few pieces of paper fall onto the floor."

14
00:01:09.754 --> 00:01:13.256
Three words and one picture fluttered through the holes in the lid.

15
00:01:14.497 --> 00:01:16.978
I picked them up and showed them to the class.

16
00:01:16.998 --> 00:01:20.180
"This is a picture of shoes," I said.

17
00:01:21.204 --> 00:01:27.028
"And there's a word on each of these pieces of paper 'sleep,' 'house,' and 'cake.'"

18
00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:29.710
Everyone just stared at me.

19
00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:32.592
"Now what do you do?"

20
00:01:33.113 --> 00:01:33.953
asked Colby.

21
00:01:33.973 --> 00:01:38.056
"Well," I said, not entirely sure.

22
00:01:38.076 --> 00:01:40.978
"Now you—" "Ooh!"

23
00:01:41.459 --> 00:01:42.159
cried Gina.

24
00:01:42.179 --> 00:01:45.081
"That gave me a great idea, Iggy!

25
00:01:45.602 --> 00:01:48.224
My story is about a fox and a hunter.

26
00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:52.458
The fox wants to stop the hunter from hunting in the woods.

27
00:01:53.618 --> 00:01:59.501
Now I know what the fox can do—wait until the hunter is sleeping.

28
00:02:00.902 --> 00:02:05.605
Then the fox can sneak into the hunter's house and steal his shoes.

29
00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:09.287
Without shoes, the hunter can't go hunting.

30
00:02:10.347 --> 00:02:15.930
At the end of the story, Fox and the other animals will celebrate with cake!"

31
00:02:17.451 --> 00:02:19.132
Everyone was amazed.

32
00:02:20.636 --> 00:02:22.357
I could hardly believe it either.

33
00:02:23.217 --> 00:02:25.057
My plot inventor worked!

34
00:02:26.538 --> 00:02:30.239
All the kids lined up to take turns using the plot inventor.

35
00:02:31.299 --> 00:02:35.760
Pretty soon everyone was writing, and no one was stuck anymore.

36
00:02:37.921 --> 00:02:42.742
Mrs. Romano said the plot machine was one of the best inventions she'd ever seen.

37
00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:48.304
"Iggy, may I let the other fourth-grade class use it for their stories?"

38
00:02:49.064 --> 00:02:49.724
she asked.

39
00:02:50.688 --> 00:02:51.969
Proudly, I told Mrs.

40
00:02:52.029 --> 00:02:54.091
Romano that was just fine.

41
00:02:55.211 --> 00:02:59.935
Earlier I said that no one was stuck on their stories anymore, but that wasn't quite true.

42
00:03:01.176 --> 00:03:05.559
There were two people who were still stuck: Molly and me!

43
00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:12.684
After shaking the box, we had decided to write about the giant talking vacuum.

44
00:03:13.765 --> 00:03:16.827
So we decided the vacuum wouldn't suck up the whole world.

45
00:03:20.296 --> 00:03:25.838
Instead the boy in the story, Jack, would use the vacuum to clean his room.

46
00:03:26.818 --> 00:03:31.440
The vacuum sucked up his bed, his clothes, and even his computer.

47
00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.760
But that wasn't all.

48
00:03:34.921 --> 00:03:37.482
The giant vacuum sucked up his older brother!

49
00:03:37.502 --> 00:03:41.803
Hmm I wonder where I got that idea!

50
00:03:43.023 --> 00:03:44.504
Our story was really funny.

51
00:03:45.444 --> 00:03:50.688
But we couldn't figure out the last part—how to get Jack's brother out of the vacuum.

52
00:03:51.649 --> 00:03:54.191
And we had to finish our stories by Friday.

53
00:03:55.512 --> 00:03:59.235
At recess Molly and I bounced ideas off some other kids.

54
00:04:00.496 --> 00:04:04.600
"Jack could just leave his brother inside the vacuum," suggested Jake.

55
00:04:05.521 --> 00:04:08.123
I liked Jake's idea, but Molly got upset.

56
00:04:09.444 --> 00:04:10.765
"Jack wouldn't do that!"

57
00:04:11.105 --> 00:04:11.626
she said.

58
00:04:11.646 --> 00:04:14.228
"He really wants his brother back."

59
00:04:15.572 --> 00:04:19.353
"He could smash the vacuum and get his brother out," suggested Evan.

60
00:04:20.914 --> 00:04:25.855
But Molly and I both liked the giant talking vacuum, so we didn't want anyone to break it.

61
00:04:27.896 --> 00:04:33.598
When I got home, Tate yelled at me for taking the last chocolate granola bar this morning.

62
00:04:34.998 --> 00:04:39.860
By now I was ready to suck him up with a giant vacuum cleaner!
